data a_record_in_an_argv_position_becomes_its_debug_text: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_record_in_an_argv_position_becomes_its_debug_text" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: StructurallyGuaranteed, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "the capability of refusing, at the argv splice, every value that is neither a native list of strings nor the declared argv role record (std.compilers.cli_surface ProcessArgvExpansion), with a located typed refusal in place of a rendered word." } },

  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a record value reaching an argv position of a shell transport becomes ONE argv word holding its Debug text. The seed's splice (src/v1/stage0/src/v1_interpreter.rs push_shell_argv_tokens, used by dispatch_shell) expands a native List and the role record ProcessArgvExpansion, refuses the ambiguous modeled string sequence, and sends everything else to a catch-all arm that pushes format!(\"{}\", val) as a word: the interpreter value's Debug-style text, such as its type name and fields.",

    "HARM: a fabricated argument reaching a real process (DESIGN section 5: no plausible output fabricated). A caller that wraps argv words in its own sealed record, so that only one constructor can mint them, gets no splice and no refusal: the process receives a word such as the record's type and fields, which a tool may reject loudly or, for an option that takes free text, accept silently.",

    "HOW IT WAS FOUND: deciding how diagnostic.ipmi.Tool's lanplus operations take the cipher suite (gunb-ai/gunbc#15262, review 86975 and royal-koi-761's option D): a sealed IpmiCipherSuiteArgv { words } splicing a bare-name input was checked against the seed before it was built. The declaration materializer (std.operation_argv shell_materialize_operation_argv) binds the supplied list and never sees the declared type, so a witness through it would stay green while execution rendered the Debug text. The sealed type was not built; #15262 kept a word list.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the ladder (silent: no refusal, no diagnostic, a plausible argv). CEILING: structurally guaranteed -- which values may splice is decidable at the splice, so every other value has a refusal arm. NEXT TRIGGER: that refusal arm in the seed's splice, plus a RED that splices a record and must refuse; a native emission of the same splice carries the same refusal. OWNER: the seed's dispatch_shell, routed by royal-koi-761 via merry-fox-82.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
